From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] EditText: one live Editable, exact TextWatcher calls, selection, several lines

getText() returned a fresh copy of the widget's text on every call, the
selection always read as 0, a TextWatcher was told "everything changed"
after each key, and the widget was a single-line GtkText.

The text now lives in one Editable that the application gets from
getText() and may change. Changes typed into the widget and changes made
through the Editable reach the watchers once each, as
beforeTextChanged/onTextChanged/afterTextChanged with the start and
lengths of that change in UTF-16 units, and both sides show the same text
afterwards (positions cross JNI in code points). The selection is kept in
the Editable's Selection spans in both directions: setSelection, selectAll,
getSelectionStart/End and Selection.* agree with the cursor on screen.
InputFilters are applied to typed text.

The widget is a GtkTextView unless the field is single-line (singleLine,
an inputType without the multi-line flag, a password): then it stays a
GtkText, which can hide the input and reports the editor action. A touch
gives the field the keyboard focus; focus changes reach
OnFocusChangeListener.

Editable gains the methods of the interfaces it has on Android (GetChars,
Spannable, Appendable).

